// The x, in lu from the left edge of the text area, that a move up or down aims for: lhg less the left margin when a goal of the page is kept (lhg at least 0), else the pen of position lhq itself.
// By hand: with the left margin 2560, offset 5 of "BBB EEE BBB" is the second code point of line 1, at the pen 683; a kept goal of 4000 is 1440.
lay_goal(View lhv, Pos lhq, int lhg) {
  int lhx = lhg - lay_margin(lhv.doc, 3);
  if(lhg < 0) {
    lhx = lhv.doc.body.paras[lhq.para].lay.pen[lhq.off];
  }
} return int lhx;
given lg_t_text("BBB EEE BBB") ((import lp_t_v), Pos(0, 5), -1):(683)
given lg_t_text("BBB EEE BBB") ((import lp_t_v), Pos(0, 5), 4000):(1440)

// Puts in lho the position one line up (lhdir -1) or down (1) from lhq, at the offset whose pen is nearest to the goal lhg (the x of the page the caret aimed for when it started to move, -1 for the caret's own x). A caret on the first or last line stays where it is. The goal is not looked up again from the caret that results, so a short line in between does not shorten it (lay_goal is the caller's to keep).
// By hand in "BBB", "A", "BBB" (pens 0, 683, 1366 on the long lines): down from offset 2 of paragraph 0, x 1366, the short "A" gives offset 1; from there with the kept goal 3926 (1366 and the margin) the next gives offset 2 again, not 1.
lay_move_line(View lhv, Pos lhq, int lhdir, int lhg, Pos lho) {
  int lhj = lay_line_of(lhv, lhq);
  int[] lhr = [0, 0];
  lay_step(lhv, lhq.para, lhj, lhdir, lhr);
} chain (View lhv, Pos lhq, int lhdir, int lhg, Pos lho) {
  lho.para = lhr[0];
  lho.off = lay_off_at(lhv, lhr[0], lhr[1], lay_goal(lhv, lhq, lhg));
  if(lhr[0] == lhq.para && lhr[1] == lhj) {
    lho.off = lhq.off;
  }
} return void;
